.TITLE "apt"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Manages software packages on Debian-based Linux distributions. It is the primary tool for __installing__, __updating__, and __removing__ applications from the system.

.DIV "TLDR"
**apt update**
Updates the local list of available packages from the repositories.
> __update__ the update subcommand

**apt upgrade**
Installs the newest versions of all packages currently installed on the system.
> __upgrade__ the upgrade subcommand

**apt install package**
Downloads and installs a specific software package and its dependencies.
> __install__ subcommand | __package__ the name of the software

**apt remove package**
Removes an installed software package while keeping its configuration files.
> __remove__ subcommand | __package__ the name of the software

**apt purge package**
Removes a package and deletes all of its configuration files.
> __purge__ subcommand | __package__ the name of the software

**apt search keyword**
Searches for a specific keyword in the names and descriptions of available packages.
> __search__ subcommand | __keyword__ the term to search for

.DIV "SUMMARY"
You must run most __apt__ commands with __sudo__ to have the necessary permissions for system-wide changes. It is a good habit to run __apt update__ before performing any installations or upgrades to ensure you are getting the latest versions.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**cli:dpkg** **cli:apt-cache** **cli:apt-get**

